{"role":"assistant","content":"Исправления внесены. Теперь полное сквозное тестирование. Подниму локальный мок Intervals.icu (только localhost, внешние сервисы не трогаю) — он воспроизводит строгую проверку `redirect_uri`, выдаёт токены в двух вариантах (как у Rivera без `expires_in`/`refresh_token`, и с ними) и умеет отвечать 401:","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_0YOOTUIP2w83vh5vnRiZ643u","function":{"name":"Write","arguments":"{\"content\":\"#!/usr/bin/env python3\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Local mock of the Intervals.icu OAuth/API endpoints (loopback only).\\n\\nMimics the behavior captured in logs/connect-attempt.log:\\n- /oauth/authorize answers 400 invalid_request when the query string is not\\n  fully form-encoded (raw ':' inside the redirect_uri value), like the real\\n  provider did since the calendar scopes were added.\\n- /api/oauth/token issues tokens; code \\\"code-rivera\\\" returns the Rivera-style\\n  body (no expires_in, no refresh_token), other codes return expires_in and a\\n  refresh_token. A refresh_token of \\\"rt-*\\\" rotates and returns expires_in=3600.\\n- /api/v1/athlete/<id>/wellness returns 401 for access token \\\"dead-token\\\",\\n  200 otherwise.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport json, threading, time\\nfrom http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer\\nfrom urllib.parse import parse_qsl, urlsplit\\n\\nSTATE = {}\\n\\n\\ndef split_raw(query):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Parse a query string the strict way: values must be %-encoded.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    out = {}\\n    for pair in query.split(\\\"&\\\"):\\n        k, _, v = pair.partition(\\\"=\\\")\\n        out[k] = v\\n    return out\\n\\n\\nclass Mock(BaseHTTPRequestHandler):\\n    def log_message(self, *a):\\n        pass\\n\\n    def reply(self, code, obj):\\n        body = json.dumps(obj).encode()\\n        self.send_response(code)\\n        self.send_header(\\\"Content-Type\\\", \\\"application/json\\\")\\n        self.send_header(\\\"Content-Length\\\", str(len(body)))\\n        self.end_headers()\\n        self.wfile.write(body)\\n\\n    def do_GET(self):\\n        url = urlsplit(self.path)\\n        if url.path == \\\"/oauth/authorize\\\":\\n            raw = split_raw(url.query)\\n            decoded = dict(parse_qsl(url.query))\\n            # strict check: no reserved character may appear raw in a value\\n            for name in (\\\"redirect_uri\\\", \\\"scope\\\", \\\"state\\\"):\\n                val = raw.get(name, \\\"\\\")\\n                if any(ch in val for ch in \\\":+=\\\"):\\n                    return self.reply(400, {\\\"error\\\": \\\"invalid_request\\\"})\\n            if decoded.get(\\\"client_id\\\") != \\\"tricoach-dev\\\":\\n                return self.reply(400, {\\\"error\\\": \\\"invalid_request\\\"})\\n            redir = decoded[\\\"redirect_uri\\\"]\\n            state = decoded.get(\\\"state\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n            self.send_response(302)\\n            self.send_header(\\\"Location\\\", f\\\"{redir}?code=code-rivera&state={state}\\\")\\n            self.end_headers()\\n            return\\n        if url.path.startswith(\\\"/api/v1/athlete/\\\") and url.path.endswith(\\\"/wellness\\\"):\\n            auth = self.headers.get(\\\"Authorization\\\", \\\"\\\")\\n            if auth == \\\"Bearer dead-token\\\":\\n                return self.reply(401, {\\\"error\\\": \\\"invalid_token\\\"})\\n            return self.reply(200, [{\\\"id\\\": \\\"2026-11-07\\\", \\\"restingHR\\\": 48}])\\n        self.reply(404, {\\\"error\\\": \\\"not found\\\"})\\n\\n    def do_POST(self):\\n        url = urlsplit(self.path)\\n        if url.path == \\\"/api/oauth/token\\\":\\n            body = self.rfile.read(int(self.headers.get(\\\"Content-Length\\\", 0))).decode()\\n            fields = dict(parse_qsl(body))\\n            if fields.get(\\\"grant_type\\\") == \\\"refresh_token\\\":\\n                if not fields.get(\\\"refresh_token\\\", \\\"\\\").startswith(\\\"rt-\\\"):\\n                    return self.reply(400, {\\\